WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When Barack Obama was
in office,

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
you received criticism
from the Left.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.673
Now with Trump in office,
you´re receiving criticism

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the Right.
Is part of that

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.876 size:84% position:42%
that you don´t believe
it´s your job to parrot

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
what a President is saying,
and do you feel like right now

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
we´re seeing a lot
from media figures?

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like -- Yes.
First of all,

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
our job is to hold
them accountable

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.419
and hold them responsible
and point out when they´re lying

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
and point out when
they say things that can´t

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
possibly be true,
and be aggressive.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:25.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
We´re not supposed to be
their friends.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know,
it´s pretty simple.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:31.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for eight years, I was not
President Obama´s friend,

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now I´m not
President Trump´s friend.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But it´s weird because

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:40.073
a lot of people on the Right
in the media these days...

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:41.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are, first of all,
I should point out,

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:43.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of very
intellectually-honest

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.311
conservatives that I see, like,
at "The Weekly Standard,"

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:48.148
at "The National Review."

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:50.417
There are some people on
the Right, and the media Right,

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
that think it is
somehow rebellious

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:55.722 size:88% position:44%
to be displaying fealty,

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:58.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
and cozying up to power,
to the President,

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.727
and it just seems so odd to me,
because that´s --

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.696
It wasn´t cool when people on
the Left did that to obama,

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it´s not cool when people
on the Right do it

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
to President Trump.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I agree with that.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.235
You also do something that --

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.337
We´ve talked about it before
on the show, state of the union,

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
you also do
"State of the Cartoonian."

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:13.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which is sort of
the week´s news

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.077
via cartoons that you draw.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.244
-Yeah, I´m a failed cartoonist.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are a failed cartoonist.
-Yeah.

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:22.849
-I did not realize that
cartooning in your younger days

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:25.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
got you in trouble,
in high school.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
We tracked down a pretty
good story about you.

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:31.124
-So, let me just preface this
story by saying to my father,

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:35.462
who is watching, I still don´t
think it´s good that I did this.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:37.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:41.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
I understand that
I made a mistake.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:44.938
So, I was one of the kids
in high school that was kind of

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:46.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
a wise guy.
-Sure.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:49.843
-And so, you know, they have
those ads in the yearbook,

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.911
in the back of the yearbook.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:53.746
You remember "Mad Magazine" has
the fold in?

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:54.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:57.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we had a fold...
-It would be like, yeah...

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Instead of folding it out,
you fold it in,

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.888
and so it was this big ad

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the Morgan Stearns
of Wynnewood

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.325
congratulating the school
in it´s fortieth year,

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it had "Fortieth Year"
in big letters,

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:12.866
and when you folded it in,
it became an appendage...

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
that only men have.
-Yeah.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-And boys.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But this was definitely

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:18.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
a man´s, okay?

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it said,
"For all the B.S.,

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
eat this."

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.882
And you managed to do this
in a way that was not --

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:30.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
They did not
recognize it until...

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, and I had
some co-conspirators.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did it, and then I had
some co-conspirators

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:36.156 size:78% position:39%
on the yearbook staff
who, like, you know.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And how quickly
were you found out?

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.759 size:84% position:42%
-The day of graduation.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:42.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I guess that´s
the safest day to get out.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.164
-But, before we graduated.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.598
-Oh, so that´s not great?

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
So we got punished,

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.234
and we walked down the aisle.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.003
We got empty naugahyde folders,

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we had to do
community service,

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.339 size:88% position:44%
and we had to apologize.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.475
Although, our apology was great.

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:58.378
It was before we even new what a
Washington, D.C. Apology was,

00:02:58.378 --> 00:02:59.579
and we wrote one of those.

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "I´m sorry if
anybody was offended...

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:05.618
...you delicate creatures."
-I actually saw that apology,

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
and when you folded that in,
it was also a [bleep].

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:09.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:12.992 size:84% position:42%
-We thought about that.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.427
-Yeah, that would have been...

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:15.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks so much
for being here, man.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s always such
a pleasure to see you,

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you´ve got
to come back soon.

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.166 size:84% position:42%
Jake Tapper, everybody.

